Z||000018||DecadenceR||08-09-2001||02:37 AM||||BACKSEAT DRIVER<P>A taxi passenger tapped the driver on the shoulder to ask him  <BR>something. The driver screamed, lost control of the car, nearly <BR>hit a bus, went up on the footpath, and stopped centimeters from <BR>a shop window. For a second everything went quiet in the cab, <BR>then the driver said  <P>"Look friend, don't ever do that again. You scared the daylights <BR>out of me!"  <P>The passenger apologized and said he didn't realize that a little <BR>tap could scare him so much.  <P>The driver replied "Sorry, it's not really your fault. Today is <BR>my first day as a cab driver - I've been driving a hearse for  <BR>the last 25 years."<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||84Bill||08-09-2001||08:25 AM||||Kinda icky joke<P>A man walks into a bar looking very depressed, The bartender asks "what do ya want" the man replies coke. The bartender was surprised to hear such a request and asks the man if he wants a shot of burbon with that. The man replies 'no, see I was out partying last night and when I got home I ended up blowing chunks so I'm giving up drinkin for good' The bartender says "hey man everyone overdoes it from time to time, it's fairly common to blow chunks when you over do it." The man looks at the bartender with a deeper look of desperation then looks back down at the bar top and says "Thats not the problem. You see, chunks is my dog"||||reg||1
